@crew halloran-emeka
// Emeka Halloran (he/him), Works systems officer, days. The Works writer, batch 2. Warm; terrible jokes; "lovely".

== greet
? tier=stranger
- {hi}. You'll be new. Have you eaten? Breakfast's in the mess till eight.
- {hi}. Emeka Halloran, systems. Tea corner's behind the parts racks, if you need me.
? tier>=acquaintance time:morning
- {hi}. Why did the scrubber go to the infirmary? It had a filter cough.   #funny
- {hi}. I had a joke for you. I've lost it. That's probably for the best.   #funny
? tier>=colleague
- {hi}, {me}. Sit down a minute. You look like you've been standing since Tuesday.
? tier>=friend
- {me}. Lovely. I saved you a scone. Don't tell Brennan where it came from.   #warm

== bye
- {bye}. And eat something, mind.
- {bye}. Tea's at half ten. You know where.

== feel
? mood:low
- No joke today. Don't look at me like that. I'll have two tomorrow.
? mood:high
- Brennan let me have an oven on Saturday. A whole oven. I'm still glowing.   #funny

== near
? act:work
- Board's tidy, rota's done, kettle's on. Lovely. Now, what's broken?
? act:breakfast
- Just made it. I always just make it. The joke takes the time.   #funny

== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- I trade breakfast jokes with Yoon. Mine are worse. It's not a contest. It is a bit.   #funny
? tier>=colleague
- I swapped my days off so Torres could meet you. Best swap I ever made.   #warm

== joy
? tier>=acquaintance
- The face people make at a warm scone. That's why I bake. Well, that and the scone.

// ---- Day 5, Friday: the new hand's mug at Works tea (week 1; facts.md section 9). Halloran gives it. After that,
// flag:mug (onboarding sets it) means your mug hangs on the tea corner rack.
== week1
? week1:true weekday:thu
- Works tea tomorrow at half ten. Don't be late. There's a reason. I can't say.   #funny
? week1:true weekday:fri
- Here. Your mug. Your name on it and everything. Welcome to Works, properly.   #warm
- Every new hand gets a mug on their first Friday. It's the law. Well, it's me.   #funny
- Hook's the one on the end of the rack. Yours from now on. Nobody else touches it.
? flag:mug
- Your mug's still on the rack. I gave it a rinse. Don't tell anyone I'm soft.   #funny

// ---- Writer 2, batch 1: to ~30 (greet by time and warmth, near, invite, accept, decline, missed, birthday, cue)
// He never says no (his thread): his declines are yeses postponed.
== greet
? tier>=acquaintance time:afternoon
- {hi}. Afternoon slump. I've a joke for it. No? Fair. Have you eaten, at least?
? tier>=acquaintance warmth:cold
- {hi}, stranger. Have you been eating? You've been somewhere. Sit. Tell me.

== near
? place:teacorner
- Kettle's on, mugs on the rack, rota on the wall. All's right with the world.
? habit:garden-lover
- The tomatoes are coming on. I check them every day. They don't seem to mind.
? habit:music
- Music room most evenings now. I sit at the back and tap my foot. Badly.   #funny

== invite
? tier>=acquaintance
- Works tea, half ten, tea corner. Bring yourself. I'll find you a mug.
- Come and see the tomatoes after shift? The garden's lovely in the evening.

== accept
- Lovely. Yes. I'll bring something baked. I'll bring two somethings.   #funny
- Yes. I was going to say yes before you finished asking.   #funny

== decline
- I'd love to. I can't. I've said yes to three people tonight. Tomorrow? Please?
- Not tonight, I'm covering the rota. I'm always covering the rota. Next time.

== missed
- I kept you a scone. It's a bit sad now. I'll eat it. For you.   #funny

== birthday
? birthday:you
- Happy birthday! I baked. I told Brennan it was an emergency. It was.   #funny
? birthday:me
- My birthday. I baked my own cake. Is that sad? It's a very good cake.   #funny

== cue
? cue:repair.you@dept
- Saw your job on the board. Done, signed, closed. Lovely. Have a biscuit.   #warm
